// PENDING: `self.cells[self.i].hp` — a RUNTIME-indexed record element's
// field, read as a store value — retains no scalar expression row, so the
// entry's Unit plan is omitted at `structural field store: pure source:
// scalar expression row` and the program is refused with the downstream
// symptom, "selected ProgramEntry establishment rejoins 0 Terminal
// attachment identities".
//
// Both halves already work; only their composition is missing. Measured as
// a three-line control matrix over the same program:
//
//   self.scratch = self.plain[self.i];      scalar element, runtime index  OK
//   self.scratch = self.cells[0].hp;        record field, literal index    OK
//   self.scratch = self.cells[self.i].hp;   record field, runtime index    OMITTED
//
// So this is compositional lowering rather than a new producer family: the
// runtime index is already planned for a scalar element, and the field
// projection is already planned under a literal index.
//
// It was built, all four layers, and what remains is a TERMINAL VOCABULARY
// choice rather than another gate. 04 produces the read already —
// `CheckedScalarExpression::StructuralParameterIndexedRead` carries an
// `element_path` — behind one line in `values/scalar/scalar_lowering.rs`'s
// `view_element_field_read`, `if !selection.through_view`. Lifting it, then
// carrying the element path through 05's `prepare_expression`, walking it
// to its scalar leaf in `primitive_store::lower_indexed_path`, and
// appending it after the `RuntimeIndex` segment at emission, reaches
// Terminal validation — which refuses with `InvalidPrimitiveScalarRead`.
//
// No current Terminal operation can spell this read, by exhaustion:
//
//   PrimitiveScalarRead { source, path }
//       admits a RuntimeIndex segment, but the Field arm of
//       `primitive_projection_type` steps only into a STRUCTURAL child, so
//       the path cannot end at a scalar leaf field.
//   IntegerStructuralField { source, path, field }
//       names the scalar leaf separately — it is what `self.cells[2].hp`
//       emits, and that program builds and exits 70 — but its path is
//       canonical, and canonical spelling exists to exclude runtime
//       selection.
//   ElementViewRead { source, index, path }
//       carries an index AND an element path, the right shape, but its
//       source is a view, so the carrier path is empty.
//
// So the choice is between giving `IntegerStructuralField` a runtime index,
// giving `ElementViewRead` a carrier path, and letting a
// `PrimitiveScalarRead` path end at a scalar field. Terminal Psi is the
// portable boundary, so that belongs with its product contract rather than
// a lowering patch.
//
// Two samples wait on it, and both write the loop form rather than the
// literal one: `samples/cli/collections/entity_list`
// (`self.scratch = self.monsters[self.i].hp;`) and
// `samples/cli/rendering/bouncing_particles` (`self.a = self.ps[self.pi].x;`).
// Promote to `pass/collections/` with an exit when it lands.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Cell { hp: i32; }

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    cells: [Cell; 4];
    i: u64 [0..=3];
    scratch: i32;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    self.i = 0;
    self.scratch = self.cells[self.i].hp;
    self.console.exit_process(self.scratch);
}
